[Event "Black Repertoire 01: Dragon - Yugoslav 9.Bc4"]
[Site "Tarrasch"]
[Date "2026.10.14"]
[Round "1"]
[White "Yugoslav Attack 9.Bc4"]
[Black "Repertoire (Black)"]
[Result "*"]

{The Sicilian Dragon: fianchetto the bishop on g7 where it rakes the long
diagonal towards b2 and White's queenside king. Black's weapons: the half-open
c-file, ...Ne5-c4, ...b5-b4 pawn storm and the famous exchange sacrifice
...Rxc3! White's plan in the Yugoslav: Be3, Qd2, f3, O-O-O, then h4-h5 and Bh6
to trade the Dragon bishop. It's a race - whoever attacks faster wins!}
1.e4 c5 2.Nf3 d6 3.d4 cxd4 4.Nxd4 Nf6 5.Nc3 g6 6.Be3 Bg7 7.f3 O-O 8.Qd2 Nc6
9.Bc4 Bd7 10.O-O-O Rc8 11.Bb3 Ne5 12.Kb1
(12.h4 {The Soltis Variation: meet h4 with ...h5! to slow White's attack.}
12...h5 13.Bg5 Rc5 14.Kb1 b5 {Black's queenside attack is fast. Watch for
...Rxc3 and ...Nc4.})
12...Nc4 13.Bxc4 Rxc4 14.g4 b5
{Black's queenside pawns roll forward (...b4, ...Qa5), and ...Rxc3 is always in
the air. Remember: the Dragon bishop is your best piece - never trade it
cheaply.} *

[Event "Black Repertoire 02: Dragon - Yugoslav 9.O-O-O"]
[Site "Tarrasch"]
[Date "2026.10.14"]
[Round "2"]
[White "Yugoslav Attack 9.O-O-O"]
[Black "Repertoire (Black)"]
[Result "*"]

{Against 9.O-O-O strike in the centre at once with 9...d5! This is the most
direct and thematic answer.}
1.e4 c5 2.Nf3 d6 3.d4 cxd4 4.Nxd4 Nf6 5.Nc3 g6 6.Be3 Bg7 7.f3 O-O 8.Qd2 Nc6
9.O-O-O d5 10.exd5 Nxd5 11.Nxc6 bxc6 12.Bd4
(12.Nxd5 cxd5 13.Qxd5 {Greedy!} 13...Qc7 14.Qxa8 Bf5 15.Qxf8+ Kxf8 16.Rd2 h5
{For the exchange Black has a ferocious attack on the white king with ...Rb8,
...Qb6 and the two bishops.})
12...Bxd4 13.Qxd4 Qb6 14.Na4 Qc7 15.Bc4
{Black plays ...Be6/...Bf5 and ...Rab8 with easy, active play along the b-file
towards White's king.} *

[Event "Black Repertoire 03: Dragon - Classical 6.Be2"]
[Site "Tarrasch"]
[Date "2026.10.14"]
[Round "3"]
[White "Classical 6.Be2"]
[Black "Repertoire (Black)"]
[Result "*"]

{Calmer for both sides. Black develops quickly and plays on the queenside with
...Rc8, ...a6, ...b5, or in the centre with ...d5 when possible.}
1.e4 c5 2.Nf3 d6 3.d4 cxd4 4.Nxd4 Nf6 5.Nc3 g6 6.Be2 Bg7 7.O-O O-O 8.Be3 Nc6
9.Nb3 Be6 10.f4 Qc8
{...Bc4 to trade White's good bishop, ...Rd8 and ...d5. If White plays f5, the
e5 square is yours.} *

[Event "Black Repertoire 04: Dragon - Levenfish 6.f4"]
[Site "Tarrasch"]
[Date "2026.10.14"]
[Round "4"]
[White "Levenfish 6.f4"]
[Black "Repertoire (Black)"]
[Result "*"]

1.e4 c5 2.Nf3 d6 3.d4 cxd4 4.Nxd4 Nf6 5.Nc3 g6 6.f4 Nbd7
(6...Bg7 $2 {A known trap!} 7.e5 dxe5 8.fxe5 Nfd7 9.e6 {White's attack is
very strong.})
{Covers e5 so that e4-e5 doesn't work.}
7.Nf3 Bg7 8.Bd3 O-O 9.O-O
{Black continues ...Nc5 hitting d3/e4, ...a6, ...b5. Solid and active.} *

[Event "Black Repertoire 05: Dragon - 6.Bc4"]
[Site "Tarrasch"]
[Date "2026.10.14"]
[Round "5"]
[White "6.Bc4"]
[Black "Repertoire (Black)"]
[Result "*"]

{Club players often play 6.Bc4 with Be3 and O-O. Learn the fork trick
...Nxe4 + ...d5!}
1.e4 c5 2.Nf3 d6 3.d4 cxd4 4.Nxd4 Nf6 5.Nc3 g6 6.Bc4 Bg7 7.h3 O-O 8.O-O Nc6 9.Be3 Nxe4 10.Nxe4 d5
{The fork trick! ...d5 hits Bc4 and Ne4, and the g7 bishop eyes d4. Black wins
back the piece with a great position.} *

[Event "Black Repertoire 06: Dragon - Fianchetto 6.g3"]
[Site "Tarrasch"]
[Date "2026.10.14"]
[Round "6"]
[White "6.g3"]
[Black "Repertoire (Black)"]
[Result "*"]

1.e4 c5 2.Nf3 d6 3.d4 cxd4 4.Nxd4 Nf6 5.Nc3 g6 6.g3 Nc6 7.Nde2 Bg7 8.Bg2 O-O
9.O-O Rb8
{...b5-b4 to chase the c3 knight and open the queenside.} *

[Event "Black Repertoire 07: Anti-Sicilian - Alapin 2.c3"]
[Site "Tarrasch"]
[Date "2026.10.14"]
[Round "7"]
[White "Alapin 2.c3"]
[Black "Repertoire (Black)"]
[Result "*"]

{Hit e4 straight away with ...Nf6. After e5 Nd5 Black gets quick development
and pressure on White's centre.}
1.e4 c5 2.c3 Nf6 3.e5 Nd5 4.d4 cxd4 5.Nf3 Nc6 6.cxd4 d6 7.Bc4 Nb6 8.Bb5 dxe5
9.Nxe5 Bd7
{Black trades White's strong e5 knight and plays ...e6, ...Be7, ...O-O with an
isolated pawn target on d4.} *

[Event "Black Repertoire 08: Anti-Sicilian - Smith-Morra"]
[Site "Tarrasch"]
[Date "2026.10.14"]
[Round "8"]
[White "Smith-Morra 2.d4 cxd4 3.c3"]
[Black "Repertoire (Black)"]
[Result "*"]

{Decline the gambit with 3...Nf6 - it transposes to the Alapin structure and
avoids all of White's traps.}
1.e4 c5 2.d4 cxd4 3.c3 Nf6 4.e5 Nd5 5.cxd4 d6 6.Nf3 Nc6 7.Bc4 Nb6 8.Bb5 dxe5
9.Nxe5 Bd7 10.Nxd7 Qxd7 11.Nc3 e6
{Comfortable for Black: White's d4 pawn is isolated and a long-term target.} *

[Event "Black Repertoire 09: Anti-Sicilian - Grand Prix / Closed"]
[Site "Tarrasch"]
[Date "2026.10.14"]
[Round "9"]
[White "2.Nc3 / 2.f4"]
[Black "Repertoire (Black)"]
[Result "*"]

1.e4 c5 2.Nc3 Nc6 3.f4
(3.g3 {Closed Sicilian.} 3...g6 4.Bg2 Bg7 5.d3 d6 6.Be3 Rb8 7.Qd2 b5
{Queenside pawn storm while White plays on the kingside.})
3...g6 4.Nf3 Bg7 5.Bc4 e6 6.O-O Nge7 7.d3 d5 8.Bb3 O-O
{Black blunts the c4 bishop with ...e6/...d5 - White's attack runs out of
steam.} *

[Event "Black Repertoire 10: Anti-Sicilian - 2.f4 Grand Prix"]
[Site "Tarrasch"]
[Date "2026.10.14"]
[Round "10"]
[White "2.f4"]
[Black "Repertoire (Black)"]
[Result "*"]

1.e4 c5 2.f4 d5 3.exd5 Nf6
{Hit back in the centre at once. Black regains the d5 pawn with active
pieces.} *

[Event "Black Repertoire 11: Anti-Sicilian - Moscow 3.Bb5+"]
[Site "Tarrasch"]
[Date "2026.10.14"]
[Round "11"]
[White "Moscow 3.Bb5+"]
[Black "Repertoire (Black)"]
[Result "*"]

{Trade bishops and play in the centre with ...e6 and ...d5.}
1.e4 c5 2.Nf3 d6 3.Bb5+ Bd7 4.Bxd7+ Qxd7 5.O-O Nc6 6.c3 Nf6 7.Re1 e6 8.d4
cxd4 9.cxd4 d5 10.e5 Ne4
{Good French-like structure where Black's bad bishop is already traded.} *

